  "$id": "https://contracts.omnivia.dev/application/v1/operations.schema.json",
  "title": "OmniVia Core Application Contract v1 - operation metadata and catalogue",
  "description": "The declared contract characteristics of one operation: its scope, payload schemas, required capability, side effects, and job/pagination/idempotency/precondition/audit/error posture. `x-omnivia-operation-catalogue` is the canonical catalogue of the twenty v1 application operations, materialized against `OperationMetadata`; the Python and TypeScript catalogues are generated from it, so it is the single source and no hand-maintained second catalogue exists. `service.health`, `service.readiness`, and `service.discover` are dedicated runtime probes (`service.schema.json`) and are deliberately not catalogue operations. Publishing the catalogue binds contract metadata only: no handler, dispatch, authorization, storage, durable-job execution, or transport behaviour is defined here. This document declares no root type; apart from the catalogue annotation it is a definition container only.",
